  "body": "From https://github.com/whatwg/streams/issues/139#issuecomment-49204030:\n\n> In `ReadableStream`, not declaring completion of `start` by returning a pending promise affects `[[callPull]]`. It's delayed until completion of `start`. `start` being pending in `WritableStream` doesn't affect `write`. `write` can invoke `[[advanceQueue]]` even if `start` is not finished. Maybe we want to make it affect something? For example:\n> 1. keeping the `state` `waiting` until `start` completes\n> 2. preventing `[[advanceQueue]]` being executed until `start` completes\n> \n> I think we want to do 2.\n",
